Subject: [PATCH 0/5] media: qcom: camss: Add Milos camera subsystem support

This series adds RDI capture support for the Qualcomm Milos (SM7635)
camera subsystem, as used by the Fairphone 6.

The hardware has four CSIPHYs, three CSIDs and three TFE665 instances.
Rather than duplicating the VFE-340 driver, the series introduces variant
data for the BUS offset, RDI packer format and write-master count. The
existing TFE530 keeps its previous values; TFE665 selects its own values
and the existing 16-byte bytesperline alignment.

The remaining patches document qcom,milos-camss, add the CSIPHY v2.2.1
D-PHY register sequence and describe the SM7635 resources, including
per-PHY regulator loads. Only the three RDI lines per TFE are exposed.
The TFE665 PIX pipeline differs from TFE530 and is not enabled here.
C-PHY support and the other FP6 cameras are outside this series.

The OV13B10 binding/driver additions and Milos/FP6 DTS changes are sent as
separate series. They are needed together for the FP6 ultra-wide capture
path, but are not prerequisites for applying these CAMSS patches.

Testing of the earlier enablement revision on a temporary Milos 7.2
kernel included all six OV13B10 modes, nine matching CSID/VFE/RDI routes,
start/stop and module reload cycles, and a 9,600-frame full-resolution
stress capture. This is not a claim of boot testing the current upstream
base. Host-side checks of the revision prepared on 2026-09-06 included an
ARM64 Clang W=1 CAMSS object build and focused binding/example validation.

Thanks to Jorijn van der Graaf for the suggestions reflected in the
individual patches.

